Hi all,

This is to announce that sysstat 9.0.4 has been released and is 
available for download.

This version fixes a nasty memory corruption bug in sadc. Huge thanks to 
Jonathan Kamens for pinpointing it. Apart from that, other changes here 
are really small stuff.

Sysstat 9.0.4 is available for download from my web page at:
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

288kB sysstat-9.0.4.tar.gz
235kB sysstat-9.0.4.tar.bz2
292kB sysstat-9.0.4-1.src.rpm
249kB sysstat-9.0.4-1.i586.rpm

It will also be available on ibiblio Linux archive site in a few days:
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/system/status/

The sysstat utilities are a collection of performance monitoring tools 
for Linux. These include sar, sadf, mpstat, iostat, pidstat and sa 
tools. Check out http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/features.html
to get a view of sysstat's main features.
Feedback always welcomed. Send your remarks and comments to:
sysstat <at> orange <dot> fr.

To learn some more about sysstat, check out
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

Enjoy!

Changes vs 9.0.3 are:
* [Jonathan Kamens]: Fix double free/memory corruption bug with sadc.
* [Jeroen Roovers]: Get entirely rid of implicit rule for libsyscom.a in 
Makefile to fix a problem with parallel execution.
* sysstat.ioconf configuration file updated.
* NLS updated.
* CREDITS file updated.

